The hosted site and any signed-in browser; the CI Linux runner beyond what the PR's job logs show; the `python` and `package` jobs of CI (their reads are checked statically in C7); the importer against real books; real price data of any kind (every figure synthetic); CodeQL queries (the PR's own run is the instrument: C8); the PR, the squash and the records rows (Tuesday's and the records seat's); any run under artificial load; the builder's mutants as its own scripts (you rebuild your own); a build of the combination with an unmerged lane; the save-time refusal of repeated numbers (not built, a decision the product owner owns; do not file it as a defect).

